{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Check account, mailbox, devices for shared mailbox issue"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0108",
  "reason": "Confirm desktop is online and healthy for Outlook troubleshooting"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the orders@ mailbox has gone missing from Outlook. Your own mailbox looks healthy and has plenty of space, so let's narrow this down:\n\n1. Fully close Outlook and open it again. Shared mailboxes usually come back on their own after a restart. If that doesn't help, restart the desktop too.\n2. Go to Outlook on the web, right-click Folders, choose \"Add shared folder or mailbox\" and enter orders@. Can you open it there?\n3. If you can open it on the web but it still doesn't show in desktop Outlook, add it by hand: File > Account Settings > Account Settings > Change > More Settings > Advanced tab > Add, then type orders@.\n\nPlease reply and tell us whether it opens in Outlook on the web. If you get an access or permission error there, your access to orders@ may have been removed. In that case the mailbox owner will need to approve access again, and we'll pass it to the team that makes that change.",
  "internal_note": "User 8 (James O'Connor, Operations, Warehouse Supervisor). Account is active, not locked and not blocked. Mailbox is at 29.7%, so quota is not the cause (KB-010). Desktop BL-DT-0108 shows offline; last check-in 2026-10-09 12:27 UTC; no warnings and plenty of free disk. I had no tool to check shared mailbox permissions on orders@, so I couldn't tell whether access was removed. Sent the user the KB-011 steps (restart Outlook, test in Outlook on the web, add the mailbox manually) and asked for the Outlook on the web result. If it fails there with an access error, the permission was likely removed: get approval from the mailbox owner and escalate to Tier 2 under KB-011/KB-006. If the user is not on the desktop, the device being offline may just be timing.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
